# Copy to torrent/gluetun.env (gitignored) and fill in, then: chmod 600 torrent/gluetun.env
#
#   cp torrent/gluetun.env.example torrent/gluetun.env
#
# THIS FILE IS A CONTRACT, NOT A DOC — the key names here are what gluetun reads.
# Same convention as duri.env.example (SPEC.md §Secrets).
#
# Get all three values from https://windscribe.com/getconfig/wireguard
# (log in → generate a WireGuard config). The generated config is an INI file;
# map it as follows:
#
#   [Interface]
#   PrivateKey = ...   →  WIREGUARD_PRIVATE_KEY
#   Address    = ...   →  WIREGUARD_ADDRESSES     ← IPv4 PART ONLY, see below
#   [Peer]
#   PresharedKey = ... →  WIREGUARD_PRESHARED_KEY ← NOT PublicKey, see below
#
# Values are NOT quoted. Compose strips surrounding quotes from env_file, but
# plain `docker run --env-file` does not — so unquoted is the form that stays
# correct everywhere. Paste the value only: no label, no ` = `.
#
# Do NOT paste the whole .conf file here, and do not commit it anywhere in this
# repo. Values move file-to-file; never echo/cat them to a console.
#
# ─── THE TWO MISTAKES THAT ACTUALLY HAPPEN (both hit on first setup, 2026-08-14) ───
#
# 1. WIREGUARD_ADDRESSES: Windscribe gives BOTH an IPv4 and an IPv6 address on
#    one comma-separated line:
#        Address = 100.72.14.9/32,fd54:4::5e2e:bbb3:7a9b:9a11/128
#    Take ONLY the IPv4 part. The box has no IPv6, and gluetun refuses to start:
#        ERROR interface address is IPv6 but IPv6 is not supported
#    This is also the safer configuration, not merely a workaround: with no IPv6
#    address in the tunnel the namespace has no IPv6 route at all, so transmission
#    cannot leak over IPv6 either — a common failure of dual-stack setups.
#
# 2. WIREGUARD_PRESHARED_KEY: the [Peer] block contains PublicKey AND
#    PresharedKey, adjacent and visually identical. You want PresharedKey.
#    Windscribe REQUIRES it; gluetun will not start without a valid one.
#
# ─── CHECK THE SHAPE WITHOUT PRINTING THE SECRET ───
#
# Both keys must be 44 base64 characters ending in "=". To verify without putting
# the values on screen (run from the repo root on the box):
#
#   awk -F'=' '
#   /^WIREGUARD_PRESHARED_KEY=/ { v=substr($0,25); k="PRESHARED" }
#   /^WIREGUARD_PRIVATE_KEY=/   { v=substr($0,23); k="PRIVATE  " }
#   v!="" { printf "%s len=%d charset_ok=%s ends_with_eq=%s\n", k, length(v),
#           (v ~ /^[A-Za-z0-9+/]+={0,2}$/ ? "yes" : "NO"), (v ~ /=$/ ? "yes" : "no"); v="" }
#   ' torrent/gluetun.env
#
# Expect `len=44 charset_ok=yes ends_with_eq=yes` on both lines. Anything else is
# the wrong field or a truncated paste.
#
# ─── AFTER EDITING THIS FILE, RECREATE — DO NOT RESTART ───
#
#   docker compose up -d --force-recreate gluetun transmission
#
# Env vars are baked in at container CREATION. `restart: unless-stopped` restarts
# the same container with its ORIGINAL environment, so a fixed value here will
# appear to change nothing and you will debug an error you already fixed.
# transmission is recreated too because it lives in gluetun's namespace.

# Your 32-byte key in base64. Specific to you, and the same for every server.
WIREGUARD_PRIVATE_KEY=

# The tunnel interface address from the config, WITH the prefix length —
# e.g. 100.x.x.x/32. Also user-specific and the same for every server.
WIREGUARD_ADDRESSES=

# Windscribe REQUIRES this to be set (gluetun's Windscribe docs are explicit).
# It has a real value in the generated config — copy it.
WIREGUARD_PRESHARED_KEY=
